  "title": "Critique: people overestimate the richness of what they see",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "ef0726b2-cb7d-4083-9d64-889c411081d0",
      "text": "When letters in a Sperling display are replaced by pseudo-letters, or a scene is scrambled across a blank, observers still report seeing letters or no change. They overestimate the content of their own experience.",
